Sentinel — Critical Security Repair & UX Overhaul

You are working on Sentinel, a Discord server security bot implemented in Python.

Your task is to audit, repair, test, and improve the existing security system, logging infrastructure, observation engine, security posture analyzer, and anti-nuke setup wizard.

This is a functional repair task, not merely a UI redesign. Several features currently appear configured but do not perform their intended actions in real Discord servers.

1. Critical Requirements

Prioritize the work in this order:

1. Restore real Discord logging.
2. Fix emergency lockdown so it performs and verifies actual permission changes.
3. Fix the logging setup wizard so it creates real Discord channels.
4. Repair the security observation engine and event detection.
5. Fix security posture calculation and refresh behavior.
6. Redesign the anti-nuke setup wizard.
7. Implement a unified Quick Setup / Advanced Setup security wizard.
8. Make all relevant commands support prefix and slash invocation consistently.
9. Simplify buttons, messages, error handling, and the overall UI.
10. Add regression tests and verify the fixes against the actual SDK implementation.

Do not simply modify configuration flags, add placeholder implementations, or report success because a database record was created.

A configured feature must actually work. A successful operation must be verified.

